{"chunk_id": "2e15b1216214", "text": "Duryodhana urges his father Dhritarashtra to invite the Pandavas to a gambling match, arguing that dice involve no violence and could reduce the Pandavas\u2019 superiority. Though Dhritarashtra senses the immorality and danger of the scheme\u2014and recalls Vidura\u2019s earlier warnings\u2014he resigns himself to fate and orders the construction of a magnificent crystal-arched assembly hall where the game will occur. The dazzling palace is swiftly built, and Vidura is sent to summon Yudhishthira. Troubled, Vidura warns that gambling breeds misery and could destroy the Kuru line, but the king insists the invitation be delivered. When Vidura reaches Yudhishthira, the Pandava king immediately suspects quarrel and danger in a dice game. This moment sets the tragic machinery in motion: political envy, moral hesitation, and fatalism combine to lead the Kurus toward catastrophe.\nDuryodhana persuades Dhritarashtra to invite the Pandavas to a gambling match; despite Vidura\u2019s warnings, the king orders a grand hall built and summons Yudhishthira.\nThemes: fate vs free will, deception and gambling, ignored counsel, family rivalry", "vector": [-0.0004764731856994331, -0.01439330168068409, -0.0046656252816319466, 0.010950836353003979, -0.033340416848659515, 0.015531755052506924, -0.026008235290646553, -0.0006175092421472073, -0.02291814796626568, -0.018147487193346024, 0.017930638045072556, 0.009378686547279358, 0.017388518899679184, 0.016060322523117065, -0.007210203912109137, 0.023866860195994377, 0.039141107350587845, -0.0027580384630709887, 0.043450966477394104, -0.019543448463082314, -0.013051553629338741, -0.009399015456438065, 0.006752789951860905, 0.013248072005808353, -0.03285250812768936, 0.03919531777501106, 0.01597900502383709, -0.019367258995771408, -0.007325404789298773, 0.0011503121349960566, -0.006481729447841644, -0.009453227743506432, 0.0185540784150362, -0.007901407778263092, -0.02047860622406006, 0.02047860622406006